--- body ---
`tests/test_close.sh` has two fixture-rename operations that obscure intent:

Line ~175: `9006-suffix-closed.erg` is renamed to `9006-suffix-name-closed.erg`.
The original name already ends with `-closed` so `pathIsClosed()` would return
true on the original. The rename does not change the test outcome and makes it
unclear what property is being demonstrated.

Line ~195: `9007-disclosed-mention.erg` → `9007-disclosed-mention-keep.erg`.
Similarly, neither name affects the close logic; the rename is from a prior
iteration where name-based closing existed.

**Fix:** Remove both `mv` calls. If the test is asserting that a fixture named
`*-suffix-name-closed.erg` can still be closed normally, the fixture should
start with that name. If the intent is different, add a clear comment. Either
way, dynamic renames inside test setup make fixtures harder to trace.
